---
import InfoLayout from '../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

// TODO(owner): have this policy reviewed before launch. It must match how
// ads and consent are actually set up in AdSense when the site goes live.
const updated = '2026-09-28';
---

<InfoLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Infinite Calculators"
  description="How Infinite Calculators handles your data: calculator inputs stay on your device, how Google AdSense uses cookies, and how to opt out of personalized ads."
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  updated={updated}
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The numbers you type into our calculators are processed in your browser and are never sent to us.</li>
    <li>We don't ask you to create an account, and we don't sell your personal information.</li>
    <li>
      We show ads through Google AdSense. Google and its partners use cookies to show and measure those
      ads. You can opt out of personalized ads at any time using the links below.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers {site.name} at <a href={`${site.url}/`}>{site.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>. You can
    contact us about privacy at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What you enter into a calculator</h2>
  <p>
    Every calculator on this site runs in your web browser. Dates, amounts, measurements and other values
    you enter are not sent to our server, and we cannot see them. Closing or refreshing the page clears
    them.
  </p>

  <h2>Settings saved on your device</h2>
  <p>
    To save you choosing again on your next visit, we store a few settings in your browser's local
    storage, such as light or dark mode and your preferred units (metric or imperial). These settings stay
    on your device, are never sent to us, and can be removed by clearing your browser's site data.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like almost every website, our hosting provider (Hostinger) automatically records basic technical
    information when a page is requested: your IP address, browser type, the page requested, the
    referring page and the date and time. This is used to keep the site secure and working, and is kept
    for a limited time under the host's own retention rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google AdSense to show ads, which is how we keep the site free. Cookies are small text files
    that a website stores in your browser. When ads appear on this site:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this
      website or other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your
      visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      Other third-party vendors and ad networks may also serve ads on this site, and may use cookies,
      web beacons or similar technologies to do so.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Even if you turn off personalized ads, Google may still use cookies for non-personalized ads, for
    example to limit how often you see the same ad and to detect fraud. You can read more in
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>
    and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">how Google uses cookies in advertising</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to opt out of personalized ads</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google:</strong> turn off personalized ads in
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google's Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Other vendors (US):</strong> use the Digital Advertising Alliance's
      <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener">WebChoices tool</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Canada:</strong> use the <a href="https://youradchoices.ca/" rel="noopener">AdChoices program</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>UK and EU:</strong> use <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">Your Online Choices</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Any browser:</strong> block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking all cookies
      may stop some websites from working properly.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Visitors in the UK, EEA and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>
    If you visit from the United Kingdom, the European Economic Area or Switzerland, you will be asked
    for consent before any cookies are used for personalized ads. This consent message is provided
    through a Google-certified consent management platform, and you can change your choice at any time
    from the privacy settings link that appears with the message.
  </p>

  <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, including the UK, the EU, Canada and several US states such as
    California, you may have the right to ask what personal information is held about you, to have it
    deleted, and to opt out of its use for targeted advertising. We do not keep visitor profiles
    ourselves; advertising data is held by Google and its partners, and the opt-out tools above are the
    quickest way to control it. For any other request, email us at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information
    from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages link to other websites. Their privacy practices are their own, so please read their
    policies when you visit them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how the site handles data, for example by adding analytics, we will update this page and
    the date at the top.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
